ds important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Weak Form", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Structural words, such as prepositions, conjunctions, auxiliaries and articles are often not stressed. Some learners can find these small words difficult to hear.  This can interfere with the understanding of a sentence. The words <span class=\"strong\">in</span>, <span class=\"strong\">an</span>, <span class=\"strong\">from</span>, etc. are \u201cweak\u201d in the sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The ancient Egyptians believed in an afterlife", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The dusty rooms revealed treasures from the past.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sarcophagus ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a stone coffin from ancient times", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: The sarcophagus had not seen the sun in thousands of years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when writing information about the past.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tomb ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a building or chamber above or below the ground in which a dead body is kept ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The tomb was finally opened by his team.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gleaming ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "bright or shining ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: The gleaming artifacts shone in the sun.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dusty ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " filled or covered with dust ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The dusty room was full of antiques.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "afterlife ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a life that some people believe exists after death", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Egyptians believed in the afterlife.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The oo sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "How do you make the oo sound?</br></br>You make the oo sound by  pulling your lips into a tense, small circle. </br>The back of the tongue is raised high in your mouth.</br> The sides of the tongue can touch the top teeth at the back of your mouth.</br></br>Here are some examples: tomb, do, move, shoe, do, room", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "They discovered the tomb of the Egyptian pharaoh.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There were rooms filled with treasures.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They did not want to move the mummy.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and research archaeological discoveries in your area.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write notes that answer the questions: Who, What, When, Where and Why", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a 80-100 word paragraph on a discovery.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include 2 words with the <span class=\"italic\">oo</span> sound and two words with the short <span class=\"italic\">u</span> sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the paragraph aloud to a partner or family member.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research information about people and places.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a paragraph about archaeological discoveries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}